    bottomLine:
      "Workable in an apartment on a budget, but only with a dense rubber mat, which should be costed in from the start.",
    description:
      "The 1295i is the budget option we would still consider for an upstairs flat, with one condition attached. Its deck is firmer than the Sole machines, and firmer decks pass more impact into the floor — our downstairs readings were the highest of the full-size machines here. A dense rubber mat closed most of that gap, which is why we describe the mat as part of the purchase rather than an accessory. Nothing about the machine itself became noisy across the test: no rattles, no squeaks, no rising motor note. It is the deck, and the deck is fixable.",
